# MCL CRM frontend. Copy to .env.local for local overrides (git ignores it), or set these in the host's build
# settings. Both are read when the app is BUILT (`next build`): change them, then build again.
# Neither is a secret, and no secret belongs here: database URLs, SESSION_SECRET, SMTP and Cloudinary credentials are
# set on the API (MCL-CRM-Backend) only.

# Address of the MCL-CRM-Backend API. The Next server forwards the browser's /api/* calls there (server side: the
# browser never sees it). REQUIRED for `next build`; `next dev` uses http://localhost:4000 when it is unset.
# Production: the API's public https address, e.g. https://api.example.com (no trailing slash, no /api).
API_URL=
# Optional, public (sent to the browser): country preselected in phone fields and used to read saved numbers
# without "+code". Keep equal to the API's DEFAULT_PHONE_COUNTRY. Default IN; an empty value means no preselection.
NEXT_PUBLIC_DEFAULT_PHONE_COUNTRY=IN
